// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_wmic_terminate_application.yml
// ID Sigma: 49d9671b-0a0a-4c09-8280-d215bfd30662
// Título: Application Termination Attempt via Wmic.EXE
// Descripción: Detects an attempt to terminate a process via "wmic" with the "call terminate" flag. Adversaries may
use wmic to terminate security products or other applications on the compromised host. This event is
triggered on on attempt and process creation can be either successful or unsuccessful.

// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_wmic_terminate_application.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\WMIC.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wmic.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "call" and ProcessCommandLine contains "terminate")
